  "question": "How do I deploy my personal website in Week 2?",
  "contextNamespace": "2026-technest",
  "answer": "To deploy your personal website in Week 2 of TECHNEST 2026, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Make sure you have a working website locally by running `npm start` in your terminal.\n2. To deploy your website, you'll need to use a platform that can host your website online. One popular option is Vercel, which you can use for free.\n3. Visit the Vercel website and sign up for an account if you haven't already.\n4. Create a new project on Vercel and link it to your GitHub repository.\n5. Vercel will automatically build and deploy your website to the internet.\n6. Once deployed, you can access your website by visiting the URL provided by Vercel.\n\nAlternatively, you can also use other platforms like Netlify or GitHub Pages to deploy your website.\n\nIf you're using Her Waka 2026, you can follow the steps in the tutorial [Deploy your website](/docs/2026-her-waka/tutorial/personal-website/deploy) to put it on the internet for free!\n\nIf you have any issues or need further assistance, feel free to ask.\n\n— Reference: build website (HER WAKA 2026) (<versioned_docs\\",
